Fixed. Tests pass (3/3).

**The bug** (`src/import_merge.ts:7`): the dedup check was `b.url === inc.url`, a raw string comparison. URL scheme and host are case-insensitive, but `===` treats `https://example.com/a` and `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` as different strings, so the incoming bookmark was appended as a second entry.

**The fix**: added a `normalizeUrl` helper that lower-cases only the protocol and hostname (preserving path/query/fragment verbatim), and used it to compare both sides of the match. Non-URL strings fall back to a plain comparison.

Verified: an existing `https://example.com/a` with tag `["x"]` merged with incoming `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` with tag `["y"]` now yields a single entry with tags `["x","y"]` instead of two entries.


